  "design": "No extra GPT calls. Every 1,000-case figure is calculated from the pilot calls already measured. It is not a live 1,000-case queue. The dollar exchange uses clean single-case costs only: GPT inject-clean, and Drex inject-clean plus the two extra clean repeats on the four consistency cases. Latency and the 500 ms fraction use every single-case inject and consistency call plus those Drex repeats, and they exclude the packed batch calls. service_latency_ms is the adapter latency minus time spent inside the shared frontier rate-limit wait. latency_ms is the adapter value and includes that wait when another process is using the same 13 rpm window. The 500 ms fraction is reported on both clocks. The SLO and the serial-throughput figures use service time. On each of the four consistency cases, Drex is called two more times on the clean state (three clean asks total). A fact flips when those three choices are not all equal.",
